A: {{`Des shorts.`}}
N: CD2 piste 32, item 5. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Say “a dress” in French.
A: {{`Une robe.`}}
N: Feminine. CD2 piste 32, item 6. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Give the Québec word for “a tank top” in this clothing list.
A: {{`Une camisole.`}}
N: CD2 piste 32, item 7. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Say “a T-shirt” using the spelling in the clothing list.
A: {{`Un t-shirt.`}}
N: CD2 piste 32, item 8. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Say “a shirt” in French using `chemise` and its indefinite article.
A: {{`Une chemise.`}}
N: Feminine. CD2 piste 32, item 9. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Say “jeans” using the article and form in the manual's clothing list.
A: {{`Des jeans.`}}
N: CD2 piste 32, item 10. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Say “sunglasses” in French.
A: {{`Des lunettes de soleil.`}}
N: CD2 piste 32, item 11. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Say “a skirt” in French.
A: {{`Une jupe.`}}
N: Feminine. CD2 piste 32, item 12. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Say “winter boots” in French, with a plural article.
A: {{`Des bottes d'hiver.`}}
N: CD2 piste 33, item 1. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Say “a raincoat” in French using the word in the second clothing list.
A: {{`Un imperméable.`}}
N: Masculine. CD2 piste 33, item 2. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Give the Québec word for “a knit winter hat” with its indefinite article.
A: {{`Une tuque.`}}
N: CD2 piste 33, item 3. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Say “gloves” in French, with a plural article.
A: {{`Des gants.`}}
N: Separate fingers, unlike the mittens pictured in the exercise. CD2 piste 33, item 4. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Say “rain boots” in French, with a plural article.
A: {{`Des bottes de pluie.`}}
N: CD2 piste 33, item 5. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Give the Québec word for “sneakers” used in episode 14, with its plural article.
A: {{`Des espadrilles.`}}
N: Use the Québec meaning of the manual's clothing list. CD2 piste 33, item 6. [[fr/episode-14]]

---

Q: Say “a scarf” in French using the word beginning `foul-`.
A: {{`Un foulard.`}}
N: CD2 piste 33, item 7. [[fr/episode-14]]

